#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The Rollback workflow's "File the follow-up issue" step
# (.github/workflows/rollback.yml). Files the issue that holds the
# reason and the steps that clear DEPLOY_HOLD.
#
# Reads REASON, BAD_SHA and LIVE_SHA.
set -eo pipefail

gh issue create \
  --title "Production rolled back: $REASON" \
  --body "Production was rolled back from \`$BAD_SHA\` to \`$LIVE_SHA\` on $(date -u +%Y-%m-%d).

Reason: $REASON

The Heroku rollback is only the mitigation — main still contains the change. Until it is fixed, the \`DEPLOY_HOLD\` repository variable blocks the daily deploy.

- [ ] Fix main (usually \`git revert\` of the offending change)
- [ ] Wait for CI to go green on the fix
- [ ] Clear the hold: \`gh variable delete DEPLOY_HOLD\`
- [ ] Check whether the bad version wrote data that needs correcting entries"
